  benchmarks/dune -- no gate: its one runtest action runs python3 over the benchmark orchestrator's own unit tests, which import no OCANNL executable -- there is no startup check in reach to gate, the same reason `config_dep_completeness` exempts it from the ocannl_config dependency

Declarations of a name OCANNL does not read as a configuration key, exempt by design:
  test/operations/dune:ocannl_backedn -- the fixture behind the `config_var_warnings` golden, which captures the warning a mistyped key draws; the rule tracks the name so that an ambient one arriving does not leave the golden stale
  test/operations/dune:OCANNL_BACKEDN -- the same fixture, in the casing OCANNL reads -- a lowercase one is reported rather than read, so both write to the stream the golden holds
  test/operations/dune:OCANNL_DEMO_KEY -- a synthetic key `config_var_spellings` looks up by name: no key OCANNL reads, so it cannot be declared for its value -- but the run depends on it (gh-ocannl-749), an ambient one drawing the unknown-key warning onto the stream those goldens capture
  test/operations/dune:OCANNL_DASHED_ONLY_KEY -- the same fixture's second synthetic key, tracked for the same reason
  test/operations/dune:ocannl-log_level -- the `config_var_fatal_spelling` fixture: a known key in the dashed spelling that gh-ocannl-605 dropped, which since gh-ocannl-652 aborts the run rather than warning

Artifact-directory declarations, by dune file. A stanza whose modules call
`Test_utils.Generated.init` declares `(env_var OCANNL_BUILD_FILES_PREFIX)`
where dune runs it -- in its own `(deps ...)`, or, for an `(executable)` which has none, in
the rule that runs it (gh-ocannl-723). What is held here is which VERDICTS a file's stanzas
draw, not how many draw each: a tally would move whenever a test is added, and the per-stanza
table goes to stderr.
  the census covers every scan root, so the floor of 20 callers applies to it
  test/operations/dune: declared

Backend declarations, by dune file. Every stanza that runs an executable either declares
`(env_var OCANNL_BACKEND)`, or carries the marker comment
    ; ocannl-backend: <none|cc|multidev_cc|cuda|hip|metal> -- <reason>
inside its parentheses. What is held here is which WORDS a file's markers use, not how many
stanzas carry each: the per-stanza reasons live next to the stanzas, where the next author
will copy them from, and the tallies go to stderr (gh-ocannl-659, gh-ocannl-665).
  .claude/dune: nothing that runs a test executable
  arrayjit/lib/dune: nothing that runs a test executable
  arrayjit/test/dune: declares OCANNL_BACKEND; markers: cuda, metal, none
  benchmarks/dune: markers: none
  benchmarks/runners/ocannl/dune: markers: metal
  bin/dune: markers: cc, none
  dune: nothing that runs a test executable
  lib/dune: nothing that runs a test executable
  tensor/dune: nothing that runs a test executable
  test/config/dune: declares OCANNL_BACKEND
  test/einsum/dune: declares OCANNL_BACKEND; markers: none
  test/gpt2/dune: declares OCANNL_BACKEND; markers: none
  test/operations/atomic_file_rename_scan_fixture/dune: markers: none
  test/operations/dune: declares OCANNL_BACKEND; markers: cc, cuda, metal, multidev_cc, none
  test/operations/profiles/dune: markers: none
  test/operations/startup_streams/dune: markers: none
  test/ppx/dune: declares OCANNL_BACKEND; markers: none
  test/support/dune: nothing that runs a test executable
  test/training/dune: declares OCANNL_BACKEND; markers: cc, multidev_cc, none
  tools/dune: nothing that runs a test executable

Focused aggregate families, by dune file (gh-ocannl-783). Each family alias is spelled
identically in every directory that has members, so `dune build @<family>` from the workspace
root runs the whole family; membership is derived from what a member stanza declares, and a
member the family's `(alias (name <family>) (deps ...))` stanza omits fails this scan.
  arrayjit/test/dune: metal-codegen
  benchmarks/runners/ocannl/dune: metal-codegen
  test/operations/dune: lifecycle, metal-codegen

every stanza that runs an executable either declares the backend variable or says in place why it does not: true
every marker the text spells was read as one, and every stanza the raw text shows running an executable has a site placed for it: true
every stanza either reader names as running an executable is named by the other too: true
every focused-aggregate member is reached by its family alias, and a repository-wide derivation finds enough of them for the rule to be about something: true
every source that calls Test_utils.Generated.init is claimed by some stanza's modules, and a repository-wide census finds enough of them for the rule to be about something: true
every stanza whose modules call Test_utils.Generated.init declares OCANNL_BUILD_FILES_PREFIX where dune runs it, and every declaration of it has a caller behind it: true

Scanner refusal controls (gh-ocannl-800). Sources come from repository-wide scan rules;
controls are *_cases.expected, *_control.expected, or a live scan golden with an explicit
`Synthetic controls:` section. Printf substitutions do not decide coverage.
  statically extracted diagnostics: 385 (details on stderr)
  named exemptions with reasons:
    (none)
repository-wide scan rules resolve to scanner sources: true
the refusal-control manifest source set equals the derived scanner census: true
the permanent control-golden corpus is present: true
every statically recoverable scanner refusal diagnostic appears in a control golden or has a named reasoned exemption: true

